# r1113 chunk 4, boot A second rerun (c4_ar2): fixture fixes for the c4_ar rows judged in perf/runs/r1113/verdicts/c4_a.md
# (section c4_ar). Rows: SQ-FLR-03, -02b, -04, -05 (heated half), SQ-BREED-03, SQ-FDI-02 (which food did not count),
# SQ-FDI-03 (vanilla cake and candle cake bites).
#
# Setup: NO fresh world, no new probe. Reuse the c4_a scratch dir and world exactly as c4_ar left them (OUT = the c4_a
# scratch dir, srv = OUT/srv, level r1113c4a, the zc4 probe c4_ar copied in is unchanged). No /reload, no /dumpall.
#
# Fixes against c4_ar:
#  - SQ-FLR-03: the millstone's 9 output slots filled with 9 different ids and Create voids what does not fit
#    (MillstoneBlockEntity.process -> insertItemStacked; tick only halts on a FULL slot). Now a hopper under the millstone
#    drains it into a chest, the millstone is driven by a cogwheel beside it (it is an ICogWheel) at 32 rpm, and the chest
#    is counted.
#  - SQ-FLR-02b / -04: the controller existed in c4_ar but VALID was never checked (wrong spin leaves valid=false and the
#    items sit on top); the pools box only reached y -58, so items on the wheels were not even seen. Now the motors swap
#    unless the controller is valid=true, and the box covers y -63..-54.
#  - SQ-FLR-05: create:blaze_burner placed without a state is blaze=none = the EMPTY burner (no block entity, so tryInsert
#    returned FAIL). Now placed as blaze=smouldering. Only the heated half reruns (the unheated half PASSed in c4_ar).
#  - SQ-BREED-03: the three bees never moved in c4_ar (same block in both readings 60 s apart, hive Bees []). Now a fresh
#    hive with the wild carrot 3 blocks away, a poppy control hive, and a bot standing between them.
#  - SQ-FDI-02: carrot=19 applepie=19 after 20 foods; read every food's has-flag on fdj (data kept in this world).
#  - SQ-FDI-03: the vanilla cake and candle cake uses returned CONSUME and recorded nothing; check whether a bite happened.
# Areas: millstone 40200, crushers 40220, mixers 40240 (z 40000 lane, as c4_ar); bees 40720-40740; cakes 40610-40616.
pace 2

## SQ-FLR-03 | Millstone: 20 flesh give exactly 20 meat items (drained into a chest)
> forceload add 40190 39990 40270 40010
sleep 3
> fill 40195 -60 39995 40205 -50 40005 minecraft:air
> setblock 40200 -61 40000 minecraft:chest
> setblock 40200 -60 40000 minecraft:hopper[facing=down]
> setblock 40200 -59 40000 create:millstone
> setblock 40201 -60 40000 create:creative_motor[facing=up]{ScrollValue:32}
> setblock 40201 -59 40000 create:cogwheel[axis=y]
sleep 3
> data get block 40200 -59 40000 Speed
expect 40200, -59, 40000 has the following block data: -?[1-9][0-9]*\.0f
> zc4 put 40200 -59 40000 biomesoplenty:flesh 20
waitlog \[zc4\] done 20
expect \[zc4\] put 40200 -59 40000 biomesoplenty:flesh inserted=20
sleep 150
> zc4 inv 40200 -59 40000
waitlog \[zc4\] done 20
> zc4 poolsinv 40200 -61 40000
waitlog \[zc4\] pools by id 20
count \[zc4\] pools meat=20 bone=\d+ eye=\d+ misc=\d+ >= 1
reject \[zc4\] inv 40200 -59 40000 total=\d+ .*biomesoplenty:flesh x
look the chest pools line: meat=20 exactly, flesh used up (millstone inv line empty or near empty); bone near 15, eye near 5, misc near 5; the hopper itself may still hold up to 5 stacks (zc4 inv 40200 -60 40000 by hand if meat is 15-19)

## SQ-FLR-02b | crushing wheel rig: controller forms AND is valid (setup for SQ-FLR-04)
> execute if block 40221 -58 40000 create:crushing_wheel_controller[valid=true] run say FLR crusher valid before swap
> execute if block 40221 -58 40000 create:crushing_wheel_controller[valid=false] run say FLR crusher invalid before swap
> execute unless block 40221 -58 40000 create:crushing_wheel_controller[valid=true] run setblock 40220 -58 39999 minecraft:air
> execute unless block 40221 -58 40000 create:crushing_wheel_controller[valid=true] run setblock 40222 -58 40001 minecraft:air
> execute unless block 40221 -58 40000 create:crushing_wheel_controller[valid=true] run setblock 40220 -58 40001 create:creative_motor[facing=north]{ScrollValue:128}
> execute unless block 40221 -58 40000 create:crushing_wheel_controller[valid=true] run setblock 40222 -58 39999 create:creative_motor[facing=south]{ScrollValue:128}
sleep 5
> execute if block 40221 -58 40000 create:crushing_wheel_controller[valid=true] run say FLR crusher valid ok
expect FLR crusher valid ok
> data get block 40220 -58 40000 Speed
> data get block 40222 -58 40000 Speed

## SQ-FLR-04 | Crushing wheels: 100 pus bubbles about 25 slimeballs, 100 hair about 50 string, nothing else
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item,x=40215,y=-64,z=39995,dx=12,dy=12,dz=10]
> summon minecraft:item 40221.5 -56.5 40000.5 {Item:{id:"biomesoplenty:pus_bubble",Count:64b}}
sleep 25
> summon minecraft:item 40221.5 -56.5 40000.5 {Item:{id:"biomesoplenty:pus_bubble",Count:36b}}
sleep 40
> zc4 pools 40221 -59 40000 -4
waitlog \[zc4\] done 20
> summon minecraft:item 40221.5 -56.5 40000.5 {Item:{id:"biomesoplenty:hair",Count:64b}}
sleep 25
> summon minecraft:item 40221.5 -56.5 40000.5 {Item:{id:"biomesoplenty:hair",Count:36b}}
sleep 40
> zc4 pools 40221 -59 40000 -4
waitlog \[zc4\] done 20
count \[zc4\] pools meat=0 bone=0 eye=0 misc=0 slime=(1[5-9]|2\d|3[0-5]) string=0 other=0 >= 1
count \[zc4\] pools meat=0 bone=0 eye=0 misc=0 slime=0 string=(3[5-9]|[4-5]\d|6[0-5]) other=0 >= 1
look first pools line ~25 slime only, second ~50 string only; pus_bubble / hair under "others" means the wheels did not take (or not all of) the stack

