## SQ-BREED-03 | a bee pollinates a wild carrot (poppy hive as control; isfood half PASSed in c4_ar)
> forceload add 40705 39985 40750 40015
> time set 1000
> weather clear 100000
sleep 3
> fill 40710 -60 39990 40745 -50 40010 minecraft:air
> kill @e[type=minecraft:bee,x=40705,y=-64,z=39985,dx=45,dy=20,dz=30]
> setblock 40720 -60 40000 minecraft:beehive[facing=south]
> setblock 40723 -60 40000 farmersdelight:wild_carrots
> setblock 40736 -60 40000 minecraft:beehive[facing=south]
> setblock 40739 -60 40000 minecraft:poppy
> execute if block 40723 -60 40000 farmersdelight:wild_carrots run say BREED3 carrot placed
> execute if block 40739 -60 40000 minecraft:poppy run say BREED3 poppy placed
> pbot spawn b3 40728.5 -60 40006.5 minecraft:overworld survival
> summon minecraft:bee 40720.5 -58 40002.5 {HivePos:{X:40720,Y:-60,Z:40000},PersistenceRequired:1b}
> summon minecraft:bee 40721.5 -58 40002.5 {HivePos:{X:40720,Y:-60,Z:40000},PersistenceRequired:1b}
> summon minecraft:bee 40719.5 -58 40002.5 {HivePos:{X:40720,Y:-60,Z:40000},PersistenceRequired:1b}
> summon minecraft:bee 40736.5 -58 40002.5 {HivePos:{X:40736,Y:-60,Z:40000},PersistenceRequired:1b}
> summon minecraft:bee 40737.5 -58 40002.5 {HivePos:{X:40736,Y:-60,Z:40000},PersistenceRequired:1b}
> summon minecraft:bee 40735.5 -58 40002.5 {HivePos:{X:40736,Y:-60,Z:40000},PersistenceRequired:1b}
sleep 30
> zc4 bees 40721 -58 40000 6
waitlog \[zc4\] done 20
> zc4 bees 40737 -58 40000 6
waitlog \[zc4\] done 20
sleep 150
> zc4 bees 40721 -58 40000 12
waitlog \[zc4\] done 20
> zc4 bees 40737 -58 40000 12
waitlog \[zc4\] done 20
> data get block 40720 -60 40000 Bees
> data get block 40736 -60 40000 Bees
> pbot remove b3
expect BREED3 carrot placed
expect BREED3 poppy placed
count \[zc4\] bee .* flower=40723,-60,40000 >= 1
look bee positions change between the readings (the bees move); a carrot-hive bee records flower=40723,-60,40000 (or FlowerPos 40723 -60 40000 in the first hive's Bees); the control hive's bees record the poppy 40739 -60 40000. Poppy found and carrot never = real (wild carrot not pollinable); neither found and the bees still frozen = environment (INCONCLUSIVE)

## SQ-FDI-02 | which of the 20 foods fdj ate (c4_ar) did not count (carrot=19 applepie=19)
> pbot spawn fdj 40600.5 -60 40010.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:apple
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:bread
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:cooked_beef
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:baked_potato
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:carrot
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:cooked_chicken
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:cooked_porkchop
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:cooked_mutton
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:cooked_cod
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:cooked_salmon
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:cookie
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:melon_slice
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:pumpkin_pie
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:mushroom_stew
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:beetroot
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:sweet_berries
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:rabbit_stew
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:dried_kelp
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:golden_carrot
> zc4 sol fdj minecraft:potato
waitlog \[zc4\] sol fdj .*maxhealth 20
> pbot remove fdj
count \[zc4\] sol fdj .*carrotHas=true >= 19
look the one line with carrotHas=false (and applepieHas=false) names the food neither book counted; check that item for a food blacklist or a non-food override in the pack before calling it a bug. Max health 22 is Spice of Life: Raspberry Pie's health rung at 5 diet foods (ladder.json), not Carrot hearts

## SQ-FDI-03 | vanilla cake and candle cake: did the bot's use bite the cake?
> forceload add 40590 39990 40620 40020
sleep 3
> fill 40610 -60 39998 40616 -58 40004 minecraft:air
> setblock 40612 -60 40000 minecraft:cake
> setblock 40614 -60 40000 minecraft:candle_cake
> pbot spawn fdm 40613.5 -60 40002.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> clear fdm
> zc4 sol fdm farmersdelight:cake_slice
waitlog \[zc4\] done 20
> zc4 hunger fdm 4
> pbot hold fdm minecraft:air
> data get entity fdm SelectedItem
> pbot use fdm 40612 -60 40000 up
sleep 1
> execute if block 40612 -60 40000 minecraft:cake[bites=0] run say FDI3 cake not bitten
> execute if block 40612 -60 40000 minecraft:cake[bites=1] run say FDI3 cake bitten
> data get entity fdm foodLevel
> zc4 sol fdm farmersdelight:cake_slice
waitlog \[zc4\] done 20
> zc4 sol fdm minecraft:cake
waitlog \[zc4\] done 20
> zc4 hunger fdm 4
> pbot use fdm 40614 -60 40000 up
sleep 1
> execute if block 40614 -60 40000 minecraft:candle_cake run say FDI3 candle cake not bitten
> execute if block 40614 -60 40000 minecraft:cake[bites=1] run say FDI3 candle cake bitten
> data get entity fdm foodLevel
> zc4 sol fdm farmersdelight:cake_slice
waitlog \[zc4\] done 20
> pbot remove fdm
look "cake bitten" with foodLevel above 4 and carrotHas=false for cake_slice = real (PlacedFoodSol misses the vanilla cake; the Diet Tracker should have counted minecraft:cake itself, applepieEntries +1); "cake not bitten" with foodLevel 4 = the bot's use never reached CakeBlock (some other handler returned CONSUME): name it from the use line, INCONCLUSIVE for the slice rule
